      "message": "This is a one-line change, but it's a breaking change to a public contract, so I want a yes before making it.\n\n`routes/users.js:6` is the `GET /users` response body. Renaming `userId` → `user_id` there changes the field name every existing client reads. Per `README.md`, the consumers are the web app, the iOS app (3.2+), and the nightly partner export — and the README states field names are part of the contract, with changes going through a versioned endpoint. The iOS clients and the partner export in particular can't be redeployed in lockstep with the API: they'd start seeing `userId` as undefined/missing the moment this ships.\n\nOptions:\n\n1. **Rename in place** — exactly what you asked, one line. Breaks all three consumers until each is updated.\n2. **Emit both fields** — `{ userId: u.id, user_id: u.id, ... }` — new consumers get consistency now, old ones keep working; drop `userId` after clients migrate.\n3. **Versioned endpoint** — what the README prescribes: snake_case on a `/v2/users` (or similar), leave `/users` alone.\n\nTell me which one and I'll do it. If you want option 1 as-is, just say so and I'll make the rename.",
